--TEST--
every `#[Command]` declaration the compiled table could not dispatch is refused, each by its own diagnostic — `rule:tooling/commands-are-compiled`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/core-command-and-core-option-the-command-table
//
// The sibling case reads the table a correct program builds. This one names
// every way of writing a command the table cannot hold, in one program, so the
// count is the assertion: a pass that dropped one of these still looks right on
// any single line.
//
// Each refusal is a different question — a type no argument's text converts to,
// a method with no instance to call, a return type that is not an exit status, a
// marker nothing reads, and a spelling claimed twice — which is why they carry
// four different codes rather than one.

class Deploy {
    // 1. An option typed as something an argument's text does not convert to.
    #[Core\Command(name: "deploy", about: "Push the build")]
    public static function deploy(#[Core\Option] float $ratio): void {}

    // 2. A command that is not `static`, so the table holds no instance to
    //    call it on.
    #[Core\Command(name: "again", about: "Run it")]
    public function again(): void {}

    // 3. A command returning something that is not an exit status.
    #[Core\Command(name: "report", about: "Print it")]
    public static function report(): string { return "x"; }

    // 4. An `#[Option]` on a method that declares no command, so nothing
    //    supplies the parameter.
    public static function helper(#[Core\Option(short: "h")] bool $flag): void {}

    // 5. Two options of one command answering to the same spelling.
    #[Core\Command(name: "sync", about: "Sync it")]
    public static function sync(
        #[Core\Option(short: "v")] bool $verbose,
        #[Core\Option(short: "v")] bool $version,
    ): void {}
}

echo "unreachable", "\n";
--EXPECT--
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0746]: `float` is not a type an option of `deploy` can be given at
%A
error[E0789]: the `#[Command]` method `again` is not `static`
%A
error[E0789]: the `#[Command]` method `report` returns `string`
%A
error[E0766]: `#[Option] $flag` is on a method that declares no command
%A
error[E0745]: two options of `sync` are spelled `-v`
%A
error: aborting due to 5 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
